cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Bee Geometry Tunneling
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-Francois
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374
    affiliation: Spark AI NLP
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: AGPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Quantum tunneling (Josephson-style) through a hexagonal honeycomb
  geometry -- the bee's geometry. The model reuses the measured
  per-link tunneling law of josephson-membrane v0.3.0 (each barrier
  link contributes one factor (1 - h)) and the honeycomb geometry of
  symmetry-entropy (6 neighbours, 120-degree angles, bipartite vertex
  lattice, Hales efficiency), and extends them: a 60-degree turn costs
  a factor, the critical current scales with the number of parallel
  hexagon-edge paths, and the honeycomb's symmetry axis changes the
  transmission. Synthetic and classical; no real quantum measurement
  is claimed.
keywords:
  - honeycomb
  - hexagonal lattice
  - tunneling
  - Josephson
  - bee geometry
  - synthetic
